ock and ink."},"analyst":{"role":"analyst","screenTitle":"Date Comparison","dataPayload":"ARCHIVE CLOSURE RECORD: the [ADMIN BUILDING] archive closed in 1987. No poster could have been displayed there at closure unless it was printed on or before 1987. The four poster dates are 1979, 1983, 1986 and 1991. A poster printed after the closure year could not have hung there at closure; it must have been added later.","whatTheySee":"A closure record fixed at 1987 beside four poster dates spanning 1979 to 1991.","taskPrompt":"Compare each poster date against the closure year and name the poster that post-dates it.","intermediateOutput":"P-04 (1991) falls after the 1987 closure; P-01, P-02 and P-03 do not."},"operator":{"role":"operator","screenTitle":"Acquisition Check","dataPayload":"ACQUISITION REGISTER: display approvals are logged by poster letter. P-01 approved 1979. P-02 approved 1983. P-03 approved 1986. P-04 carries no approval entry at all - it was never authorized for display at any date. Submit the letter of the poster the materials and the dates both flag: the unauthorized, post-closure insertion.","whatTheySee":"An acquisition register with approvals for three posters and a blank entry for the fourth.","taskPrompt":"Submit the letter of the poster that is both a material outlier and dated after closure.","intermediateOutput":"Awaiting the team conclusion."},"operatorInvestigation":{"operatorOwnEvidence":"The acquisition register, which approves P-01 to P-03 and holds no approval for P-04, and the closure record fixed at 1987.","operatorTaskDescription":"Confirm the flagged poster was never authorized and submit its printed letter."},"requiredDiscoveries":{"observerDiscovery":"Records all four poster letters, dates and material profiles.","analystDiscovery":"Finds that P-04 alone post-dates the 1987 closure."}}',
  answer_metadata = '{"acceptedAnswer":"F","presentedEvidence":true,"answerType":"text","caseSensitive":true,"normalization":"strip_non_alnum","validation":{"pattern":"^[A-Za-z]$","minLength":1,"maxLength":1},"fullSolution":"The archive closed in 1987. Three posters - P-01 (1979), P-02 (1983), P-03 (1986) - were printed before closure and share a single stock and ink profile; the fourth, printed 1991 on heavier, glossier stock, post-dates closure and matches no other poster. The acquisition register approves the first three and holds no approval for the fourth. That fourth poster is P-04, and its printed letter is F."}',
  metadata = '{"type":"PATTERN","difficulty":3,"time":"7m","storyReveal":"One poster was added after the building closed: its stock, its ink and its date all say so, and no acquisition entry authorises it.","locationClue":{"format":"Narrative","clueText":"Proceed to the archive figure display.","solution":"Archive Figure Display","nextPhysicalLocation":"[ADMIN BUILDING] - Archive Figure Display","nextQrNode":"QR-NODE-05","explanation":"Directs the team from the poster wall to the figure display."},"evidenceUnlocked":{"id":"EVID-P04","category":"Document","title":"Archive Poster Acquisition Register","state":"RECOVERED","timestamp":"Stage 1","source":"Archive poster wall","content":"The archive closed in 1987. Poster P-04 was printed in 1991 on stock and ink that match no other poster, and the acquisition register holds no display approval for it: it is a post-closure insertion."},"whyTeamworkMatters":"Only the observer can read the four posters'' letters, dates and materials; only the analyst can set them against the closure year; only the operator can confirm from the acquisition register that the flagged poster was never authorised.","feeds":"P03"}'
