tle":"Cross-Reference and Repository Record","dataPayload":"CROSS-REFERENCE: held below and repository point to the institution records repository - the place every pulled file is returned to. That repository floor plan is the document the team opened at the facade in Stage 1. The message is a pointer, not a farewell: it sends the team back to the plan. RECORDS OFFICE SIGNATURE BLOCK, filed under the deposits it kept: the floor plan of the institution records repository is signed and stamped, and the stamp names the repository by the archive''s own one-word term for it - the term the access register also uses.","visualType":"document-forensics","whatTheySee":"A cross-reference tying the message to the records repository, beside the repository signature block naming it.","taskPrompt":"Decide whether the message is a farewell, a warning or a pointer, and to what, then read the register''s name for that place.","intermediateOutput":"A pointer to the institution records repository, which the register names."},"operator":{"role":"OPERATOR","screenTitle":"Repository Access Register","dataPayload":"ACCESS REGISTER: the repository holds its floor plan in the access register, released to the team. The register files the repository under the archive''s own term for it, and prints that term at the head of every access line: ARCHIVE. The message points to that repository. Submit the term the register files it under.","visualType":"terminal","whatTheySee":"An access register whose every line is headed by the archive term for the repository.","taskPrompt":"Submit the archive term the register files the repository under.","intermediateOutput":"Awaiting the team conclusion."},"requiredDiscoveries":{"observerDiscovery":"Reports the window card verbatim.","analystDiscovery":"Determines the message is a pointer to the institution records repository, not a farewell, and finds the register''s name for it."}}',
